IMPORT prelude

§ `AND on two SETs is a type error — the overload was removed`

-- Until 2026-07-28 the prelude overloaded __AND__/__OR__ on SET operands
-- to mean UNION. A second candidate for these magic names made the
-- typechecker re-check argument subtrees per candidate, i.e. exponential
-- (base 3) in the DEPTH of AND/OR chains — a real 27-operand statutory
-- disjunction extrapolated to ~a year of checking (smucclaw/l4-ide#929).
-- The overloads were removed (SET-OPERATORS-SPEC §16); term-level set
-- union is spelled UNION explicitly.
--
-- This test pins the removal: AND on two SETs must fail against the sole
-- remaining candidate, the predefined boolean __AND__. If this file ever
-- typechecks again, the overloads have been reintroduced — that is only
-- legitimate if typechecker memoisation has delivered a big-O win first
-- (the §16 un-un-overloading contingency).

`new yorkers`   MEANS setFromList (LIST "alice", "bob")
`new jerseyans` MEANS setFromList (LIST "carol")

#EVAL `new yorkers` AND `new jerseyans`
